are no mandated group — 'riding' ~ 'wing' 1.000 PROMOTED_RHYME — NAMED PAIR IS NOT THE EVIDENCE: scored on: -riding [last 1 of 2 syllables of 'riding']  ~  wing   (best of k=6)","evidence":"an unintended rhyme across groups. Whether that is a defect is the writer's call and the loop does not take it: an unmandated rhyme is quite often the best thing in a song, and doctrine 7 makes this a floor rather than a ranking. It is reported because it is the one thing here that IS about the writing","locations":[14,16],"groups":[],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_COLLISION","severity":"note","message":"L15 (free) and L16 (D) RHYME and share no mandated group — 'striding' ~ 'wing' 1.000 PROMOTED_RHYME — NAMED PAIR IS NOT THE EVIDENCE: scored on: -striding [last 1 of 2 syllables of 'striding']  ~  wing   (best of k=6)","evidence":"an unintended rhyme across groups. Whether that is a defect is the writer's call and the loop does not take it: an unmandated rhyme is quite often the best thing in a song, and doctrine 7 makes this a floor rather than a ranking. It is reported because it is the one thing here that IS about the writing","locations":[15,16],"groups":[],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_UNREADABLE","severity":"note","message":"L17/L20 are mandated together (group(s) E) and the harness could not read a declared rhyme anchor, so this rhyme is UNKNOWN rather than absent","evidence":"CMUdict has no pronunciation for the end word 'xyzzq-'; the harness refuses rather than guessing one (no G2P fallback). This line's end-rhyme is UNKNOWN, not absent.","locations":[17,20],"groups":["E"],"obligations":[],"subject":["unreadable_anchor",17]},{"code":"UNREADABLE_END_WORD","severity":"note","message":"3 of 20 lines end in a word CMUdict cannot read; their end-rhyme is UNKNOWN, not absent","evidence":"No pronunciation is guessed (no G2P fallback). Every relation these lines would have entered is REFUSED and recorded, not silently dropped. Words: king-, roo-, xyzzq- SEVERITY: `readability.report` calls this a FLAG; the revision loop files it as a NOTE. A refusal is not a violation (doctrine 79), and `SCHEME_UNREADABLE` — the same refusal on a pair the mandate DECLARED — is already a note, so a flag here would fail an unmandated line harder than a mandated one. The lexicon cannot read the word; the line is not thereby wrong. `Lexicon(fallback='high'|'low')` is the declared coordinate that changes what is readable (doctrine 1) — there is no second switch for it in `ReviseDeclaration`.","locations":[9,13,17],"groups":[],"obligations":[[9],[13],[17]],"subject":[]},{"code":"SUBSTITUTED_END_WORD","severity":"note","message":"4 line(s) would have had the RHYME WORD SILENTLY REPLACED by an earlier word: L5 '2-'->'minion', L9 'roo-'->'minion', L13 'king-'->'minion', L17 'xyzzq-'->'minion'","evidence":"`word_syllable_map` emits no syllable for a word CMUdict cannot read, so anything taking its last entry as the rhyme word takes an EARLIER word instead -- the defect the shipped file carried in `_qafiya_parts`, where `zun` reported as `the` and `grow'st` as `thou`. THIS IS NOT A SECOND CHARGE. 4 of these 4 line(s) are ALREADY flagged above by UNREADABLE_END_WORD, which says the LINE cannot be read; what no other finding in this module says is WHICH WORD would have been used, and that is the only part a writer or a caller can act on -- the substitute is a plausible English word, so nothing about the output looks wrong. Every one of them is also flagged above, so this finding adds the word and no new line.","locations":[5,9,13,17],"groups":[],"obligations":[[5],[9],[13],[17]],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_UNREADABLE","severity":"note","message":"L17/L20 are mandated together (group(s) E) and the harness could not read a declared rhyme anchor, so this rhyme is UNKNOWN rather than absent","evidence":"CMUdict has no pronunciation for the end word 'xyzzq-'; the harness refuses rather than guessing one (no G2P fallback). This line's end-rhyme is UNKNOWN, not absent.","locations":[17,20],"groups":["E"],"obligations":[],"subject":["unreadable_anchor",17]},{"code":"UNREADABLE_INTERIOR_WORD","severity":"note","message":"9 line(s) are readable at the end but have an unreadable word before it","evidence":"The end-rhyme is sound. A multi-syllable anchor that reaches back past the gap (mosaic rhyme: 'spit in it') is joining phones across a hole, and the internal-rhyme and consonant-skeleton paths skip the word entirely.","locations":[2,4,6,8,10,14,16,18,20],"groups":[],"obligations":[[2],[4],[6],[8],[10],[14],[16],[18],[20]],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_COLLISION","severity":"note","message":"L1 (A) and L20 (E) RHYME and share no mandated group — 'king-' ~ 'wing' 1.000 ASSONANCE+CONSONANCE+RHYME","evidence":"an unintended rhyme across groups. Whether that is a defect is the writer's call and the loop does not take it: an unmandated rhyme is quite often the best thing in a song, and doctrine 7 makes this a floor rather than a ranking. It is reported because it is the one thing here that IS about the writing","locations":[1,20],"groups":[],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_COLLISION","severity":"note","message":"L2 (free) and L20 (E) RHYME and share no mandated group — 'riding' ~ 'wing' 1.000 PROMOTED_RHYME — NAMED PAIR IS NOT THE EVIDENCE: scored on: -riding [last 1 of 2 syllables of 'riding']  ~  wing   (best of k=6)","evidence":"an unintended rhyme across groups. Whether that is a defect is the writer's call and the loop does not take it: an unmandated rhyme is quite often the best thing in a song, and doctrine 7 makes this a floor rather than a ranking. It is reported because it is the one thing here that IS about the writing","locations":[2,20],"groups":[],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"SCHEME_COLLISION","severity":"note","message":"L3 (free) and L20 (E) RHYME and share no mandated group — 'striding' ~ 'wing' 1.000 PROMOTED_RHYME — NAMED PAIR IS NOT THE EVIDENCE: scored on: -stridi